WEBVTT

00:12.083 --> 00:13.666
Specters.

00:20.750 --> 00:23.250
They cling to their decaying privilege…

00:26.333 --> 00:28.541
and their swords.

00:31.041 --> 00:32.416
They are too arrogant…

00:34.416 --> 00:36.458
to accept defeat.

00:38.500 --> 00:41.166
They steal from the powerless.

00:43.375 --> 00:46.958
They mourn their lost dignity.

00:48.833 --> 00:50.666
Raise the cry of victory!

00:50.750 --> 00:53.583
The fools dare to rebel.

00:59.125 --> 01:02.333
Smoke signal confirmed.
It's a victory for our allies.

01:04.291 --> 01:05.958
Open fire.

01:07.041 --> 01:08.125
Sir?

01:09.041 --> 01:09.875
Fire.

01:09.958 --> 01:11.833
Our units are still behind enemy lines--

01:11.916 --> 01:13.458
Fire now!

01:16.291 --> 01:18.541
Commence firing!

01:24.541 --> 01:25.708
Aim!

01:25.791 --> 01:26.750
Fire!

01:30.125 --> 01:32.083
Stop! Stop it!

01:32.166 --> 01:33.000
It's over!

01:39.791 --> 01:42.583
Stop!

01:56.458 --> 01:58.500
Those fools…

02:00.791 --> 02:04.000
are the least fit for the new age.

02:21.166 --> 02:22.125
Such specters…

02:26.041 --> 02:28.666
must be eradicated.

02:36.291 --> 02:39.500
Gentlemen, apologies
for keeping you waiting.

03:16.250 --> 03:18.875
You've given us
such an amazing opportunity.

03:18.958 --> 03:21.041
We're the ones who should be thanking you.

03:21.125 --> 03:22.541
Indeed.

03:22.625 --> 03:25.083
Have you heard
of our family motto, Organizer?

03:25.166 --> 03:27.250
No, I'm afraid I haven't.

03:27.333 --> 03:29.958
"Never lend money to the shizoku."

03:30.041 --> 03:32.916
No one has suffered more
from their lawlessness than we have.

03:33.000 --> 03:35.541
Every time we lend them money,
they walk away with it.

03:36.125 --> 03:37.833
I don't know how we've survived.

03:38.333 --> 03:43.375
Number 159, Tekkan Ikeuchi,
fell at Kuwana-juku.

03:43.958 --> 03:47.083
Reportedly, he was killed
by number 66, Bukotsu Kanjiya.

03:49.291 --> 03:51.416
Bukotsu the Savage Slasher again?

03:51.500 --> 03:53.833
-He's a beast, through and through.
-Absolutely.

03:53.916 --> 03:56.916
But he only cares about killing,
not about making progress.

03:57.000 --> 03:58.208
Hardly worth betting on.

03:58.291 --> 04:01.125
He's nowhere near being
the first through Chiryu-juku.

04:01.208 --> 04:02.166
Exactly.

04:02.250 --> 04:06.208
-He can't die without entertaining us.
-I couldn't agree more.

04:07.125 --> 04:10.166
The real fun of Kodoku is just beginning.

04:11.208 --> 04:15.750
We've prepared plenty of entertainment
from start to finish.

04:16.333 --> 04:22.458
So let us savor the downfall of those
pathetic specters together, gentlemen.

04:24.041 --> 04:26.625
MITSUI BANK

04:36.083 --> 04:37.708
Do you despise guns?

04:39.208 --> 04:43.500
They are what buried us samurai
as the dead.

04:44.916 --> 04:46.916
No one is to blame for our fall.

04:48.250 --> 04:50.958
The times have merely changed.

04:51.750 --> 04:52.833
The times…

04:58.250 --> 04:59.458
Lower your guns.

05:00.125 --> 05:01.250
He can't focus.

06:18.916 --> 06:20.208
Move aside!

08:00.708 --> 08:02.833
-What is it? What happened?
-I heard a gunshot!

08:12.416 --> 08:13.458
Stop right there.

08:14.750 --> 08:16.125
Stop! Stop!

08:22.666 --> 08:24.083
Wait! Hey!

08:44.791 --> 08:46.875
Head to the front! Don't let him get away!

08:49.250 --> 08:50.375
Time to move!

08:50.958 --> 08:51.833
Wait!

08:52.916 --> 08:53.750
Hey!

08:54.333 --> 08:56.750
Wait! Come on!

09:58.500 --> 10:00.416
Even if you keep
pushing forward like this,

10:01.166 --> 10:03.750
there's no happiness
waiting for any of you.

10:05.208 --> 10:06.666
What's that supposed to mean?

10:07.250 --> 10:09.458
You don't need
to understand what it means!

10:16.083 --> 10:18.166
This is the end of the road for you,

10:19.125 --> 10:21.041
Kokushu Saga!

10:42.458 --> 10:43.541
Shu-nii!

10:47.750 --> 10:49.041
Come on!

11:09.791 --> 11:11.250
We shall meet again in Tokyo.

11:20.958 --> 11:21.791
Enter.

11:28.250 --> 11:30.583
We have news
from Superintendent General Kawaji.

11:31.916 --> 11:34.791
Apparently, they found nothing
at the foot of Mount Fuji.

11:34.875 --> 11:36.041
It was empty.

11:36.541 --> 11:37.791
Thank you.

11:38.625 --> 11:42.666
Lord Okubo, regarding what Maejima
mentioned before…

11:43.833 --> 11:44.750
Concerning Kawaji?

11:44.833 --> 11:45.958
Yes.

11:46.541 --> 11:49.375
Kawaji is an honorable man.

11:49.458 --> 11:52.125
-But still--
-To maintain order in this country,

11:52.208 --> 11:54.708
Kawaji traveled
as far as Europe on a study tour

11:54.791 --> 11:57.583
and established the Police Bureau himself.

12:00.750 --> 12:03.250
I do not believe that man would betray us.

12:08.458 --> 12:09.583
Those documents…

12:10.708 --> 12:12.291
May I borrow them?

12:14.250 --> 12:15.333
Can you crack it?

12:15.833 --> 12:17.833
I don't know.

12:18.333 --> 12:19.875
But I can try.

12:20.583 --> 12:24.625
I want to do whatever I can.

12:31.791 --> 12:32.958
Handle them carefully.

12:33.791 --> 12:36.083
We have no idea
where the enemy might be hiding.

12:36.791 --> 12:38.083
Thank you, sir.

12:51.583 --> 12:55.666
The one who killed Akayama
and attacked me wasn't a fake.

12:55.750 --> 12:57.458
He was a real police officer.

12:58.958 --> 13:01.750
Which means whoever's running Kodoku

13:01.833 --> 13:04.833
is connected to the Police Bureau.
Or perhaps--

13:04.916 --> 13:07.208
Someone inside the Police Bureau.

13:07.291 --> 13:08.666
That's what I'm thinking.

13:08.750 --> 13:12.291
So the Police Bureau and Mitsui Bank.

13:12.375 --> 13:14.875
It might not just be the bank.

13:15.458 --> 13:16.416
What do you mean?

13:16.500 --> 13:20.000
The zaibatsu that runs the bank
could be connected too.

13:21.125 --> 13:24.333
When you look at it that way,
it all starts to come together.

13:25.500 --> 13:27.875
The Police Bureau
monitors the participants

13:27.958 --> 13:31.875
and disposes of any dead bodies.

13:32.458 --> 13:36.708
The enormous costs needed for that
are covered by the zaibatsu.

13:36.791 --> 13:38.541
But one thing doesn't make sense.

13:38.625 --> 13:41.958
Jinbe Ando, who died first
at Tenryuji Temple,

13:42.041 --> 13:44.875
was from Kyoto Prefectural
Police Department's Fourth Division.

13:44.958 --> 13:48.125
That's right. Even the police station
Kyojin snuck into--

13:48.208 --> 13:51.958
So it's only the central Police Bureau
that is involved.

13:53.333 --> 13:55.333
Wait, but why would the police…

13:55.416 --> 14:00.875
I have no clue.
But I can tell you one thing for sure.

14:02.666 --> 14:05.666
Kodoku isn't just a simple game

14:05.750 --> 14:08.583
where the survivor walks away
with 100,000 yen.

14:09.166 --> 14:13.250
Even after reaching Tokyo,
something is bound to happen.

14:13.750 --> 14:16.541
If one of us
wants to be the last one standing,

14:16.625 --> 14:19.791
there's a chance
we may end up killing each other.

14:19.875 --> 14:22.833
Even if you're the last one left,

14:23.833 --> 14:26.375
there's no guarantee you'll return alive.

14:28.333 --> 14:29.458
How could they?

14:33.000 --> 14:34.333
But even so,

14:35.791 --> 14:37.208
I'll keep moving forward.

14:39.291 --> 14:41.500
With the little miss in tow?

14:45.500 --> 14:47.875
Maybe this is as far
as you can go with her.

14:54.916 --> 14:56.416
I'm going.

15:00.833 --> 15:02.083
Futaba…

15:04.375 --> 15:05.458
Stay quiet.

15:12.208 --> 15:16.000
Are you forgetting the one trump card
only you can play,

15:16.083 --> 15:17.916
Kokushu Saga?

15:19.708 --> 15:23.916
During the war, you were connected
to some big names in the government.

15:25.083 --> 15:27.500
How would you know that?

15:28.416 --> 15:31.833
That's our only shot
against the zaibatsu and the police.

15:35.625 --> 15:40.666
If you really care about her,
you might want to think this through.

15:57.125 --> 15:59.083
I'll be back by noon tomorrow.

16:00.041 --> 16:03.250
Take care of Futaba while I'm gone.

16:03.333 --> 16:04.500
Got it.

16:34.666 --> 16:36.875
That kind of swing won't help you.

16:41.791 --> 16:45.708
Even still. I want to become stronger.

16:48.875 --> 16:50.375
I don't want…

16:52.666 --> 16:54.791
to drag everyone down anymore.

17:09.125 --> 17:11.166
Strength isn't just about the sword.

17:15.500 --> 17:17.291
You're weak right now.

17:18.875 --> 17:20.041
You're a girl.

17:21.291 --> 17:22.333
Still a child.

17:27.791 --> 17:29.166
But that's just for now.

17:32.750 --> 17:35.583
You have to discover
a strength that is unique to you.

18:04.166 --> 18:07.500
NARUMI TELEGRAPH OFFICE

18:14.666 --> 18:15.750
How can I help you?

18:15.833 --> 18:17.583
I'd like to send a telegram.

18:18.500 --> 18:19.708
Yes, of course.

18:20.375 --> 18:24.041
Please write the recipient's name
and the message here.

18:31.125 --> 18:34.875
SPECIAL EXERCISE BY THE POLICE BUREAU

18:37.375 --> 18:38.208
Come in.

18:41.583 --> 18:43.291
-Sorry to interrupt, sir.
-What is it?

18:43.875 --> 18:47.583
We've received a suspicious telegram
addressed to the Home Minister.

18:53.166 --> 18:54.791
Kokushu Saga…

18:59.208 --> 19:00.791
I'm going to the telegraph room.

19:05.458 --> 19:08.458
I'll do it myself. Everyone out, please.

19:09.916 --> 19:10.791
Yes, sir.

19:24.500 --> 19:26.375
We've received a response.

19:27.125 --> 19:28.208
What does it say?

19:28.958 --> 19:30.708
It says, "Details, please."

19:30.791 --> 19:31.833
Who's the sender?

19:33.250 --> 19:35.000
It's from Hisoka Maejima.

19:35.625 --> 19:36.916
How is that possible?

19:37.000 --> 19:39.125
He's the closest aide
to the Home Minister!

19:40.083 --> 19:41.666
Would you mind stepping out?

19:43.166 --> 19:44.875
It's better you don't know.

19:46.625 --> 19:47.791
Oh, right.

20:10.375 --> 20:13.750
Critical incident at Tenryuji Temple.
Has it been confirmed?

20:15.625 --> 20:19.833
Report of shizoku gathering received.
Are you one of them?

20:20.416 --> 20:21.750
I am one of them.

20:22.250 --> 20:25.750
There is a child
present among the shizoku.

20:26.583 --> 20:27.791
Requesting assistance.

20:30.541 --> 20:34.041
Still investigating.
Requesting full details.

20:38.291 --> 20:39.291
Rule four.

20:39.833 --> 20:42.500
You must not speak of this game to anyone.

20:47.500 --> 20:50.500
Provide protection,
and details will follow.

20:52.125 --> 20:55.333
Police involvement is suspected.
Any information?

20:56.333 --> 20:59.541
Matter of national importance.
Details follow after protection.

21:04.666 --> 21:08.791
Meet in Okazaki in three days.
Protection to follow there.

21:11.125 --> 21:12.291
Understood.

21:21.375 --> 21:23.333
Apologies for startling you.

21:24.250 --> 21:25.833
Could you send this one too?

21:25.916 --> 21:27.000
Of course.

21:31.333 --> 21:32.250
Thank you.

21:33.083 --> 21:36.541
TO: SHINO SAGA
FROM: SHUJIRO SAGA

21:36.625 --> 21:38.208
Wait for me. Take care.

21:40.916 --> 21:42.250
I will return without fail.

21:51.291 --> 21:53.875
Kokushu Saga seems to be
one of the participants.

21:54.375 --> 21:55.458
Kokushu, you say?

21:55.958 --> 21:57.125
Yes, sir.

21:57.791 --> 21:59.291
So he's alive.

21:59.791 --> 22:02.666
He's requesting protection for a child.

22:05.041 --> 22:06.458
Any other details?

22:07.041 --> 22:09.458
When I questioned him
about police involvement,

22:09.541 --> 22:11.125
he wouldn't give a clear answer.

22:11.208 --> 22:13.416
But he called it
a matter of national importance.

22:14.541 --> 22:15.833
There's more.

22:15.916 --> 22:19.666
The Police Bureau
is mobilizing over 150 police officers

22:19.750 --> 22:22.250
and conducting exercises in secret.

22:23.208 --> 22:26.875
The Police Bureau is proceeding with
something without informing us.

22:26.958 --> 22:28.041
There is no doubt.

22:28.125 --> 22:30.166
Kawaji is the head of the Police Bureau.

22:30.250 --> 22:32.625
No one else
could maintain ties to the zaibatsu

22:32.708 --> 22:35.333
and exercise this much freedom
in controlling the police.

22:38.833 --> 22:39.791
Lord Okubo.

22:43.250 --> 22:44.375
I…

22:44.958 --> 22:46.041
I will not give up.

22:49.791 --> 22:53.083
Once Kawaji returns,
I will speak with him myself.

22:54.458 --> 22:57.208
In the meantime, speed up
deciphering the coded telegrams.

22:57.291 --> 22:59.458
Without evidence,
he'll talk his way out of it.

22:59.541 --> 23:03.000
Understood. I'll be on my way
to meet Kokushu myself.

23:03.083 --> 23:04.916
Make sure to stay alert.

23:05.416 --> 23:06.250
Yes, sir.

23:29.916 --> 23:34.041
FIREARMS - EQUIPMENT
WESTERN POLICE SYSTEM

23:34.125 --> 23:38.625
FORMATION OF A MODERN STATE POLICE

23:38.708 --> 23:40.458
TRAINING IS NECESSARY FOR EMERGENCIES

23:44.375 --> 23:45.791
Ru… Ru… Ru… Ke…

23:47.583 --> 23:48.583
One…

23:49.458 --> 23:50.791
Eleven…

23:53.291 --> 23:54.666
Eleven…

24:38.625 --> 24:39.583
Sorry for the wait.

24:39.666 --> 24:41.666
All right then, let's move.

24:41.750 --> 24:44.083
We're probably the last ones left.

24:44.166 --> 24:47.083
Most of the participants
have probably passed Chiryu by now.

24:47.166 --> 24:50.000
Better catch up,
or there won't be any wooden tags left.

24:50.583 --> 24:52.375
Right. Let's move.

25:04.750 --> 25:09.458
SEKI

25:12.458 --> 25:15.708
CHIRYU

25:17.833 --> 25:21.208
CHIRYU-JUKU
REQUIRED POINTS: 5

25:36.083 --> 25:38.416
We've been expecting you all.

25:39.083 --> 25:42.250
Saga, Katsuki, Kinugasa,
your wooden tags, sir and ladies, please.

25:42.333 --> 25:44.791
Tsuge, Sayama, this way, please sirs.

25:47.125 --> 25:49.541
Shujiro Saga, eight points.

25:50.041 --> 25:52.541
Futaba Katsuki, seven points.

25:53.166 --> 25:55.916
And Iroha Kinugasa, eight points.

25:58.291 --> 26:00.666
You are all cleared to pass Chiryu-juku.

26:00.750 --> 26:03.208
Kyojin Tsuge, seven points.

26:03.708 --> 26:06.083
You are cleared to pass Chiryu-juku.

26:07.500 --> 26:09.666
This blue tag counts for five points.

26:09.750 --> 26:11.791
Please hand over
five points' worth of tags.

26:22.875 --> 26:25.416
Sayama, your wooden tags, please.

26:34.791 --> 26:35.916
No…

26:36.000 --> 26:37.750
Futaba, let's go.

26:38.625 --> 26:39.833
Shujiro!

26:41.541 --> 26:44.291
-If we give him some of ours…
-Why bring him further?

26:44.375 --> 26:45.958
He won't make it out alive.

26:46.541 --> 26:49.125
No! Please, help him!

26:49.958 --> 26:52.458
We're barely able to survive ourselves.

26:53.250 --> 26:57.250
He's a fully grown man.
He made the decision to come here.

26:57.750 --> 27:01.291
It's his life, and he should take
full responsibility for it.

27:18.708 --> 27:19.625
Futaba.

27:22.791 --> 27:23.916
Thank you.

27:37.125 --> 27:41.125
I don't know what's going to happen.

27:43.916 --> 27:47.125
I might be killed as well.

27:50.666 --> 27:51.666
But…

27:55.291 --> 27:58.041
If I turn my back on a life
that's right in front of me,

27:58.125 --> 27:59.833
then even if I survive,

28:01.166 --> 28:03.333
I won't be able to hold my head high

28:04.166 --> 28:05.916
in front of my mother.

28:11.208 --> 28:15.291
All you're doing is prolonging a life
that is already doomed.

28:16.083 --> 28:17.958
Sayama doesn't have what it takes

28:18.041 --> 28:21.041
to be one of the nine
who might have a chance to survive.

28:25.250 --> 28:27.416
He might find another way to stay alive.

28:27.500 --> 28:29.000
That's irrelevant.

29:11.875 --> 29:14.250
Oh, well. I guess she wins.

30:15.875 --> 30:21.000
Shinnosuke Sayama, five points.
You are cleared to pass Chiryu-juku.

30:23.916 --> 30:26.666
Thank you, Futaba.

30:30.666 --> 30:31.875
Thank you!

30:32.625 --> 30:37.416
Thank you!

30:46.250 --> 30:47.541
May your journey go well.

30:53.666 --> 30:54.916
Shujiro…

30:56.666 --> 30:57.750
I'm sorry.

31:00.083 --> 31:03.750
I wouldn't have made it this far
without you, and yet…

31:04.875 --> 31:05.708
No,

31:06.250 --> 31:07.916
you're right, Futaba.

31:08.541 --> 31:10.375
We can't save everyone.

31:10.958 --> 31:13.291
But if I turn my back
on someone I can help,

31:13.791 --> 31:15.708
I'd be too ashamed to face my wife.

31:16.625 --> 31:18.750
Oh, and Futaba, nice work.

31:19.333 --> 31:20.458
Yes.

31:20.541 --> 31:22.750
Tsurubami let it slip.

31:23.625 --> 31:27.333
If we make it into the final nine,
we might have a chance to survive.

31:29.833 --> 31:32.625
You're right. He did say that.

31:33.708 --> 31:38.000
I'm sure the nine who make it to Tokyo
will be made to do something.

31:38.500 --> 31:42.791
But that doesn't necessarily mean
only one of them will make it out alive.

31:46.125 --> 31:46.958
Still…

31:47.875 --> 31:51.750
Why would the Kodoku
tell us something like that?

31:52.791 --> 31:55.958
They're not exactly on our side,
but maybe they feel sorry for us.

31:57.583 --> 31:59.083
Well, not us.

32:00.416 --> 32:01.291
You, Futaba.

32:03.125 --> 32:07.625
Who knows? You might be the one
who holds the key to Kodoku, Futaba.

32:10.041 --> 32:12.208
I've finally found a bit of hope.

32:13.041 --> 32:16.375
And it's thanks to you, Futaba.

32:47.958 --> 32:50.333
So? What was that about a samurai?

32:50.416 --> 32:53.416
I saw a samurai with a sword.

32:53.500 --> 32:55.208
He had a girl with him.

33:00.250 --> 33:01.708
Kokushu,

33:02.333 --> 33:04.375
you won't get away this time.

33:25.041 --> 33:27.833
All right, I guess this is where we split.

33:27.916 --> 33:28.875
Huh?

33:28.958 --> 33:31.458
After the mess we made
at the police station,

33:31.541 --> 33:34.500
Shinnosuke and I might be
on the wanted list by now.

33:35.041 --> 33:36.041
What?

33:36.125 --> 33:37.208
We'll split up for now

33:37.291 --> 33:40.166
and go in two groups
until the dust settles.

33:40.250 --> 33:43.083
-Will you two be okay alone?
-Who do you think I am?

33:43.166 --> 33:44.416
You watch your backs too.

33:44.500 --> 33:45.833
We'll find you later.

33:47.458 --> 33:49.125
Come on, Shinnosuke!

33:49.666 --> 33:52.666
Wait. Hold on, Kyojin!

33:54.750 --> 33:55.958
We should get going too.

34:36.333 --> 34:38.333
EUROPEAN CIPHER MANUAL

34:38.416 --> 34:40.375
To maintain order in this country,

34:40.458 --> 34:42.833
Kawaji traveled
as far as Europe on a study tour

34:42.916 --> 34:45.708
and established the Police Bureau himself.

34:59.041 --> 35:00.375
N, K…

35:02.458 --> 35:06.416
W, D, A, C…

35:07.000 --> 35:08.166
L…

35:09.875 --> 35:11.083
I…

35:48.125 --> 35:50.625
Good evening, Shinpei.

35:53.625 --> 35:54.833
Mochizuki…

35:56.375 --> 36:00.250
What brings someone from the Police Bureau
to the Home Ministry?

36:01.041 --> 36:04.666
Still working at this time of night?

36:09.750 --> 36:12.000
You shouldn't have underestimated us.

36:13.208 --> 36:16.166
Did you think we'd leave
the Home Ministry's elite unwatched?

36:18.833 --> 36:20.500
What are you really after?

36:20.583 --> 36:22.250
That's not for you to know.

36:26.333 --> 36:28.166
Almost made it.

36:30.250 --> 36:31.416
Too bad.

36:49.750 --> 36:53.250
REPORT TO KAWAJI
SAKURA AND SHUJIRO FACE-TO-FACE

37:04.750 --> 37:07.833
TO TOSHIYOSHI KAWAJI

37:13.375 --> 37:15.791
Looks like there won't be
any more developments today.

37:15.875 --> 37:17.791
Suppose it's about time to take some rest?

37:17.875 --> 37:22.708
Yes. Everyone, please rest well
in your bedrooms.

37:22.791 --> 37:26.250
I believe the results
from Chiryu will be in by tomorrow.

37:26.333 --> 37:28.541
Well then, see you all tomorrow.

37:30.541 --> 37:32.541
The Yoshida twins really are pathetic.

37:32.625 --> 37:35.916
-Okubo's secretary has been taken care of.
-Good.

37:36.000 --> 37:39.541
Still, things are getting a little hectic
at the central government.

37:40.958 --> 37:44.500
Maejima suddenly changed his schedule
and is heading for Okazaki.

37:45.000 --> 37:49.958
Evidence suggests he exchanged telegrams
from Tokyo with a Kodoku participant.

37:50.041 --> 37:51.250
Who did he contact?

37:51.333 --> 37:53.000
Number 108, Shujiro Saga.

37:59.416 --> 38:00.250
Pardon me.

38:01.375 --> 38:05.708
Gentlemen, we have a bit of a situation.z

38:07.000 --> 38:13.041
Okubo may have learned that you
and the Police Bureau are involved.

38:15.458 --> 38:16.875
What do you mean?

38:16.958 --> 38:19.291
If that's true, we could be--

38:19.375 --> 38:23.708
Please rest assured.
It's all going as expected.

38:24.250 --> 38:26.083
I have a plan.

38:26.583 --> 38:29.625
How on earth did the central government
find out who we are?

38:29.708 --> 38:34.791
It seems one of the participants leaked
information to Maejima via telegram.

38:34.875 --> 38:37.666
What? Isn't that against the rules?

38:37.750 --> 38:40.000
Number 108, Shujiro Saga.

38:40.083 --> 38:43.833
Kokushu the Manslayer… Is he disqualified?

38:43.916 --> 38:45.541
He won't be disqualified for that.

38:45.625 --> 38:46.791
But Organizer--

38:46.875 --> 38:48.708
Easy now. Let's all stay calm.

38:50.208 --> 38:51.833
According to reports,

38:51.916 --> 38:57.000
some rather intriguing participants
are starting to join Shujiro Saga.

39:00.458 --> 39:02.250
How about we let

39:03.041 --> 39:05.333
the specters fight each other

39:05.833 --> 39:08.708
to the death in Kodoku?

39:27.583 --> 39:28.916
A festival…

39:49.375 --> 39:52.791
Got a moment to chat, Gion Sansuke?

39:54.041 --> 39:55.125
Who are you?

39:55.208 --> 39:57.458
Oh, who knows?

40:02.208 --> 40:07.375
I've got no intention of fighting you,
Shikura Adashino.

40:12.916 --> 40:16.000
You guys are looking
for your siblings in Kodoku, right?

40:17.875 --> 40:20.791
Shujiro Saga and Iroha Kinugasa…

40:21.791 --> 40:24.208
Oh, and Jinroku
was there too if I'm not mistaken.

40:24.291 --> 40:25.958
What do you want from us?

40:27.666 --> 40:28.750
I wonder…

40:29.708 --> 40:32.916
Would you be interested
if your siblings were in serious trouble?

40:46.541 --> 40:49.541
Excuse me, which way is Chiryu-juku?

40:49.625 --> 40:51.416
-Pardon me?
-I think I got lost.

41:01.875 --> 41:02.958
Tell us the details.

41:20.083 --> 41:22.708
63 REMAINING

45:16.583 --> 45:19.583
Subtitle translation by: Daisy Savage
